WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.169 --> 00:00:07.577
One of the things that's extraordinary
about our executive education offerings is

00:00:07.577 --> 00:00:10.745
that the Stanford Graduate School of
Business is of course located in the heart

00:00:10.745 --> 00:00:14.060
of Stanford University, which in turn is
located in the heart of Silicon Valley.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:16.750
So this is a center of innovation.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.600
It's at the cutting edge of technology.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.920
This is where many of the brand name
startups in the world have been founded.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:28.500
And executive education programs give
our participants the opportunity

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.330
to come to Stanford, or to come and
join us if we're abroad in their location.

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:37.240
And understand what some of these
cutting edge, innovative ideas are, and

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:41.490
how they can take those ideas and
really propel their organizations forward.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:45.460
&gt;&gt; We're able to draw on all
the schools in the university, and

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:50.170
bring together experts from each of these
areas that can help us understand and

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:53.070
focus on the business problems of today.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:57.340
Our faculty here are an outstanding set
of social scientists who observe and

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:59.500
analyze the business world.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.480
And who are able to distill what
they learn from their observations

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:06.560
into actionable managerial plans and
frameworks.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:11.380
&gt;&gt; The cornerstone of our campus reads,
dedicated to the things that

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:14.620
haven't happened yet and
the people who will dream them up.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:18.057
And I think that in a nutshell
captures the essence of the GSB.

